287:{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T09:01:22.720Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"The first induction encoding confirms the hypothesis partially: program reduction and base case both prove `#Top`. The step still stalls because `evalComp` is a functional symbol with two guarded equations, and the prover does not automatically split an unknown membership Boolean.\n\nThe minimal correction is to make the standard Boolean case split explicit: one induction-step claim assumes the head contains the substring, and the other assumes it does not. Those premises are exhaustive (`P` / `notBool P`), and both retain the same recursive induction hypothesis. No trusted lemma is introduced.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
288:{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T09:01:22.721Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_049ebbe4ae2880d4016a6086dfee748195b93aab5cf880ebd9","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The first induction encoding confirms the hypothesis partially: program reduction and base case both prove `#Top`. The step still stalls because `evalComp` is a functional symbol with two guarded equations, and the prover does not automatically split an unknown membership Boolean.\n\nThe minimal correction is to make the standard Boolean case split explicit: one induction-step claim assumes the head contains the substring, and the other assumes it does not. Those premises are exhaustive (`P` / `notBool P`), and both retain the same recursive induction hypothesis. No trusted lemma is introduced."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019f8902-89b3-7df0-89ef-862c23491164"}}}
289:{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T09:01:28.200Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_049ebbe4ae2880d4016a6086e2b3a481958c40f07cbf7a9077","status":"completed","call_id":"call_AvBAVmydtlYYwmBKqenMJMwP","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /work/spec.k\\n@@\\n-                     (\\\"strings\\\" |-> SOURCE:PyList)\\n+                     (\\\"strings\\\" |-> _SOURCE:PyList)\\n                      (\\\"substring\\\" |-> SUBSTRING:String))\\n@@\\n-  claim <k> evalComp(Cons(HEAD:String, TAIL:PyList),\\n+  claim <k> evalComp(Cons(HEAD:String, TAIL:PyList),\\n                      Name(\\\"string\\\"),\\n@@\\n-    requires evalComp(TAIL,\\n-                      Name(\\\"string\\\"),\\n-                      \\\"string\\\",\\n-                      Compare(Name(\\\"substring\\\"),\\n-                              CmpOp(\\\"in\\\", Name(\\\"string\\\"))),\\n-                      (\\\"strings\\\" |-> SOURCE)\\n-                      (\\\"substring\\\" |-> SUBSTRING))\\n-             ==K filterRef(TAIL, SUBSTRING)\\n-    [label(UNIVERSAL-STEP)]\\n+    requires containsString(HEAD, SUBSTRING)\\n+             andBool\\n+             (evalComp(TAIL,\\n+                       Name(\\\"string\\\"),\\n+                       \\\"string\\\",\\n+                       Compare(Name(\\\"substring\\\"),\\n+                               CmpOp(\\\"in\\\", Name(\\\"string\\\"))),\\n+                       (\\\"strings\\\" |-> SOURCE)\\n+                       (\\\"substring\\\" |-> SUBSTRING))\\n+              ==K filterRef(TAIL, SUBSTRING))\\n+    [label(UNIVERSAL-STEP-KEEP)]\\n+\\n+  claim <k> evalComp(Cons(HEAD:String, TAIL:PyList),\\n+                     Name(\\\"string\\\"),\\n+                     \\\"string\\\",\\n+                     Compare(Name(\\\"substring\\\"),\\n+                             CmpOp(\\\"in\\\", Name(\\\"string\\\"))),\\n+                     (\\\"strings\\\" |-> SOURCE:PyList)\\n+                     (\\\"substring\\\" |-> SUBSTRING:String))\\n+          => filterRef(Cons(HEAD, TAIL), SUBSTRING)\\n+        </k>\\n+    requires notBool containsString(HEAD, SUBSTRING)\\n+             andBool\\n+             (evalComp(TAIL,\\n+                       Name(\\\"string\\\"),\\n+                       \\\"string\\\",\\n+                       Compare(Name(\\\"substring\\\"),\\n+                               CmpOp(\\\"in\\\", Name(\\\"string\\\"))),\\n+                       (\\\"strings\\\" |-> SOURCE)\\n+                       (\\\"substring\\\" |-> SUBSTRING))\\n+              ==K filterRef(TAIL, SUBSTRING))\\n+    [label(UNIVERSAL-STEP-DROP)]\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019f8902-89b3-7df0-89ef-862c23491164"}}}
